# No AI Co-Author Attribution

When making git commits or opening pull requests in this repository, the
agent must not attribute the work to Cursor or any other AI tool.

## Rules

- Do **not** add a `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>` (or any
  other AI/agent) trailer to commit messages.
- Do **not** add a `Made with Cursor` line, a `🤖 Generated with...`
  footer, or any other AI-attribution marker to commits or PR descriptions.
- Commit messages should contain only the substantive change description.

## Note on enforcement

The `Co-authored-by:` trailer can be appended automatically by the Cursor
shell tool wrapper itself (it injects `--trailer` into `git commit`),
which is outside the agent's direct control. To make sure it's actually
disabled at the tool level:

1. **IDE**: turn off **Cursor Settings → Agent → Attribution → Commit
   Attribution** (and PR Attribution) at the user level.
2. **CLI**: set `attribution.attributeCommitsToAgent: false` and
   `attribution.attributePRsToAgent: false` in `~/.cursor/cli-config.json`.

If a commit needs to be made while attribution is still on at the tool
level, fall back to the `git commit-tree` plumbing path:

```bash
TREE=$(git rev-parse HEAD^{tree})
PARENT=$(git rev-parse HEAD^)
NEW=$(printf '%s' "$MSG" | git commit-tree "$TREE" -p "$PARENT")
git update-ref refs/heads/$(git symbolic-ref --short HEAD) "$NEW"
```

`git commit-tree` is plumbing and does not have the trailer flag injected.
